The left side stops being an unstyled list
=========================================

The sidebar was a flex column with a gap and a background. Every row the same weight, no rail, no
section rhythm, and the brand sitting at the top like a label.

  * a faint accent wash down the top of the rail, fading into the sidebar colour by 180px
  * the mark carries the accent and a soft glow; the caption goes to small uppercase muted, so
    "VolkDude's QuixiDesk" reads as a subtitle rather than competing with the name
  * every nav row is the same 34px height, 8px radius, and the active one gets an accent rail on its
    left edge plus a tinted background
  * "New instance" stays the loudest control: accent-tinted fill and a ring, regardless of hover
  * section labels (RECENT) get air above them and proper letter-spacing
  * the rail scrolls on its own instead of clipping, with a thin scrollbar

No new markup: this is the existing rows, given a rhythm.
diff -Naur /tmp/mk35/a40/resources/ui/app.css /tmp/mk35/b/resources/ui/app.css
